      "blurb": "The hip's ball and socket can pinch its cartilage rim (labrum) in deep flexion and rotation, causing a sharp groin 'pinch' with squats, long sitting, and pivoting, common in active younger adults. Hip shape changes and labral tears are common on scans in people with no pain, so scans are only part of the picture.",
