      "clin": "Greater trochanteric pain syndrome: gluteal tendinopathy with or without bursitis (Grimaldi 2015)",
      "blurb": "The tendons of the buttock muscles, where they attach at the bony point of the outer hip, become sensitive to load and to pressure; a nearby fluid cushion (bursa) can be involved too. It is the classic 'can't lie on that side' hip, most common in women between 40 and 60, and in runners.",
