      "blurb": "A small fluid sac sits in front of the kneecap to let the skin glide over it. A lot of kneeling, or a knock, can irritate it so that it fills with fluid into a soft swelling on the front of the kneecap. It is common in people who kneel for work. A hot, red or very tender swelling needs a doctor, as it may be infected, even without a fever.",
