      "blurb": "The spinal cord in the neck can be gradually squeezed, most often by age-related changes in the discs, joints and ligaments. Because the cord carries messages between the brain and the body, the first signs are often in the hands and legs rather than the neck. This is not a reason to panic, but it is a reason to get checked promptly.",
